\fs32 \cf2 Accessing the memory\'97to retrieve or update a value\'97is called dereferencing the pointer. You can dereference a pointer by following the variable name with an empty pair of square brackets:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf6 \cb13 # Update an initialized value\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf14 \cb13 ptr\cf5 []\cf14  \cf5 +=\cf14  \cf15 10\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb13 # Access an initialized value\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb13 print(\cf14 ptr\cf5 [])\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

