\fs32 \cf2 The following function uses the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/unsafe_pointer/UnsafePointer/#strided_load"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul strided_load()}} and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/unsafe_pointer/UnsafePointer/#strided_store"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul strided_store()}} methods to invert the red pixel values in an image, 8 values at a time. (Note that this function only handles images where the number of pixels is evenly divisible by eight.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb13 def\cf14  \cf23 invert_red_channel\cf5 (\cf14 ptr\cf5 :\cf14  UnsafePointer\cf5 [mut=\cf15 True\cf5 ,\cf14  UInt8\cf5 ],\cf14  pixel_count\cf5 :\cf14  Int\cf5 )\cf14  raises\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     \cf6 # number of values loaded or stored at a time\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     \cf5 comptime\cf14  simd_width \cf5 =\cf14  \cf15 8\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     \cf6 # bytes per pixel, which is also the stride size\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     bpp \cf5 =\cf14  \cf15 3\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     \cf5 for\cf14  i \cf5 in\cf14  \cf23 range\cf5 (\cf15 0\cf5 ,\cf14  pixel_count \cf5 *\cf14  bpp\cf5 ,\cf14  simd_width \cf5 *\cf14  bpp\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         red_values \cf5 =\cf14  \cf5 (\cf14 ptr \cf5 +\cf14  i\cf5 ).\cf14 strided_load\cf5 [\cf14 width\cf5 =\cf14 simd_width\cf5 ](\cf14 bpp\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         \cf6 # Invert values and store them in their original locations\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         \cf5 (\cf14 ptr \cf5 +\cf14  i\cf5 ).\cf14 strided_store\cf5 [\cf14 width\cf5 =\cf14 simd_width\cf5 ](~\cf14 red_values\cf5 ,\cf14  bpp\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
